# Scratch workspace for agent-driven development runs (ledgers, briefs, reports).
# Never part of the repo: the git history is the durable record.
.superpowers/

# Wave 6 content-migration artifacts (REDESIGN-2.0 §11.4).
#
# The NDJSON a migration script emits, and the rollback id lists derived from
# it, are GENERATED and deterministic: `node scripts/migrate-<family>.mjs`
# rebuilds them byte for byte from `content/**`, and every migration script is
# tested for exactly that property. Committing them would put a second copy of
# the whole content corpus in the history, in a format nobody reads, that goes
# stale the moment a content file changes and that no test would catch.
#
# The DIFF REPORTS beside them (`docs/migration/*.md` and their `.json`
# sidecars) are deliberately NOT ignored. They are the audit record the wave
# gate is written against, they name the gaps a reader needs, and they are
# small.
/docs/migration/artifacts/
#
# The same two generated shapes are also ignored wherever else under
# `docs/migration/` a script writes them, because the five Wave 6 agents did
# not all settle on `artifacts/` and a rule that only covers one directory
# would silently start committing corpus dumps the first time one of them
# changed its default output path.
/docs/migration/**/*.ndjson
/docs/migration/**/*-rollback-ids.txt
